 ## When the copy of a lead stage to the CRM fails
 
-The copy of a lead's stage (and owner) to the CRM is tried again, not given up at once: after a failed try the desk waits 10, 60, 180 and then 420 seconds before the next one (five tries in all, about 11 minutes, counted on the desk's own clock, so after a restart the next try happens immediately; the number of tries already made is kept, so the waits continue from that point and the five tries in all still apply). After the fifth failure the desk gives up on that stage: the lead's side panel shows the chip "Not copied" with a note, and the desk does not try again by itself. Only a later stage restarts the copy: moving the lead to a later step (by hand, or the automatic step after the follow-up) resets the count. A lead that already is at the last stage has no later step, so it is not copied again; the note says so. The waits (10, 60, 180 and 420 seconds), the five tries and the giving up are tested in `tests/test_mirror_gate.py` (with a fake clock). The chip "Not copied" and its notes are tested in `tests/test_stage_confirm_browser.py` and `tests/test_mode_safety.py`; the count going back to 0 on a later step is tested in `tests/test_mode_safety.py` (the test that a new stage starts the copy again after a give-up). No test restarts the desk during a wait, so the sentence about a restart is not tested.
